.TH ZEX-UPGRADE 1 "2026-06-27" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex-upgrade \- upgrade userland or syshub packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elevate zex uland --u
.br
.B elevate zex syshub --u
.SH DESCRIPTION
Upgrade is exposed only as two commands (no bare
.BR "zex upgrade" ):
.B zex syshub
and
.BR "zex uland" .
The engine is also used by
.BR "zex update" .
Sub-modes:
.TP
.B uland \-\-u
Upgrade all userland packages (T1\(enT4). Reads the current index,
diffs against installed versions, downloads and installs upgrades.
.TP
.B syshub \-\-u
Upgrade the immutable syshub base. Assembles the new base in
.I /overlayer/syshub.new/
and performs an atomic rename swap to the live path.
.PP
Pinned packages are skipped automatically in both modes.
.PP
For a full system update including index refresh, use
.B zex update
instead.
.PP
.B syshub
upgrades are crash-safe: each checkpoint is journaled to disk and marked
with an atomic state file, so an interrupted upgrade (power loss, kill
-9) is detected and rolled back automatically the next time any
.B zex
command runs, before it touches anything else.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zex-update (1),
.BR zex-rollback (1),
.BR zex-history (1)
